@startuml M6-Crawl-Activity

' Crawl operation activity flow: from seed file to stored documents
' Shows all steps: load seeds -> fetch API -> parse -> deduplicate -> store
' Includes error handling and retry logic

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam activityBorderColor #333
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam arrowColor #333
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - Crawl Operation Activity Flow

start
:Load seed file
(list of repos);
:Parse repository
owner/name pairs;

repeat
  :Get repo from queue;
  
  :Fetch metadata from
  GitHub API;
  
  if (Success?) then (yes)
    :Download README
    markdown content;
    
    if (README exists?) then (yes)
      :Check if repo
      already indexed;
      
      if (Already crawled?) then (yes)
        :Skip (deduplication);
      else (no)
        :Mark as seen;
        :Create document
        object;
        :Store in M4
        (KV Store);
        
        note right
          Document includes:
          - repo name/owner
          - README content
          - star count
          - programming language
          - topics/tags
        end note
      endif
      
    else (not found)
      :Log warning;
      :Skip repo;
    endif
    
  else (failed)
    :Increment retry
    counter;
    
    if (Retries < 3?) then (yes)
      :Wait (exponential
      backoff);
      :Re-queue repo;
    else (exceeded)
      :Mark as failed;
      :Log error;
    endif
  endif
  
repeat while (More repos?)

:Crawl complete
(N repos fetched);
:Report stats:
- repos crawled
- repos failed
- duplicates skipped;

stop

note right
  Performance targets:
  - Fetch rate: ~10 repos/sec
  - Total crawl time: 5-10 seconds
    for 100 repos
  
  Bottleneck: GitHub API
  rate limit ~60 req/min
  (with auth: 5000 req/hr)
end note

@enduml
